          "body": "**DRAFT. Do not merge until Sean publishes 1.7.0 and `npm view @hyperdag/trustshell version` returns 1.7.0.** This PR carries the site install strings.\n\n#557 (immune-system hardening) is merged, and XC1 marked it SAFE-TO-RELEASE in round 3. This head is rebased on main with #552–#557 and carries XC1's two S3 follow-ups:\n- A grounded release no longer prints the word VERIFIED. `released_by` now reads `(quote found: <reason>, page N)`.\n- CLI `--help` says `--check hal` asks only the default backend.\n\n**Final head:** `4bc3bf865b66208e6399f7316e542daa9d5efc1a`. It changes only CHANGELOG.md compared with `65723321`, the head the gate below ran on; code and dist are identical.\n\n## What 1.7.0 adds vs 1.6.1\nSee the CHANGELOG, dated 2026-10-16. Every line in it names the code or test that makes it true.\n- **Immune system v0 (#553, #557):**\n  - `remember` stores notes untrusted unless you pass `--trusted`, and even `--trusted` text is screened for injection.\n  - Notes from 1.6.1 open as quarantined `legacy`.\n  - A ground release against the recorded source makes a note `grounded`.\n  - A two-family HAL release on the default endpoint makes it `verified`.\n  - There is no release over MCP.\n  - What it does not claim: sandboxing or adaptive behaviour.\n- `ground`, `groundQuote` / `groundClaims` and `ground_quote` (#548, #549).\n- `receipt`, `kernelReceipt()` and `kernel_receipt` (#543).\n- `check` and `check_claim` keep the engine's approximate-arithmetic answer (#556).\n- Extension parity (#554). The extension is not in the tarball.\n- The docs say \"since 1.7.0\" everywhere. On a clean 1.6.1 install, each labelled surface exits 2 as an unknown option or command [V].\n\nNot cited as release evidence: #552's on-chain gate is weaker than its MEASURED wording, and a follow-up PR is fixing it.\n\n**Known limit (no change needed):** `releaseByHalWith` ships under `dist/` and can be loaded by absolute path. That is covered by the README line \"Not a boundary against code in your own process\".\n\n## Release gate on the final head [V]\nPacked tarball (105 files, 226.1 kB), installed in a clean directory, no key set.\n\n**Library**\n- All 13 new exports are present, and `releaseByHalWith` is not exported.\n- `releaseByHal` takes only `(id, opts)`; opts holds just a timeout.\n- `TrustShell.init()` reports health ok. `verifyOutput` returns Paris PASS 100 and Rome VETO 0.\n- `getRepID` returns 2236 ESTABLISHED. `presentProof` verifies.\n- `groundQuote` returns VERIFIED on the right page and VETO on the wrong one.\n- Releasing a note against itself as source is NOT_CHECKED. Releasing against the recorded source works and gives `grounded`, with no \"verified\" in `released_by`.\n\n**CLI**\n- `--version` prints 1.7.0.\n- `check` on the sentence vetoes (exit 1). `check` on the run URL completes.\n- `verify` returns PASS. `repid`, `proof --verify` and `badge` all work.\n- `ground` returns VERIFIED (exit 0) and VETO (exit 1).\n- `receipt` with no key exits 3.\n- Quarantine:\n  - default `remember` stores the note quarantined; `--trusted` stores it and `recall` prints it;\n  - `list` shows no text;\n  - a self-sourced release is NOT_CHECKED with `source_mismatch`;\n  - a release against the recorded source makes the note `grounded`;\n  - `release --trusted` works;\n  - an injection pasted with `--trusted` is quarantined, and it is printed 0 times by `recall --include-quarantined`;\n  - the `--help` line for `--check hal` names the default backend.\n\n**MCP, run alone**, both through the installed bin and through `npx -y -p <tarball>`:\n- 19 tools, and no `quarantine_release`.\n- `remember` stores the note untrusted, with `source_recorded: true`.\n- `quarantine_list` carries no note text.\n- `ground_quote` returns VERIFIED. `kernel_receipt` with no key returns 401.\n\n**Tests:** full jest on this head passes apart from two groups. The known Windows env set (CRLF and paths, plus live-network smoke) fails. The timing ceilings in `scrub-email` and `scrub-pem` fail under load and pass when run alone. `check:doc-version` reports VERIFIED.\n\n## XC1 bounded check: measured items [V] on `4bc3bf86`\n- The CHANGELOG edges bullet now says what `tests/ground-xc1.test.ts` shows: a JavaScript number past 2^53 is not checked; the same digits as a string still verify; a different digit string is a VETO (:81-107). Each other item in that bullet now cites the lines of its own test.\n- `npm run check:doc-version`: **VERIFIED**. package.json is 1.7.0; it walked 127 markdown files and found no current-version claim that contradicts it.\n- `npm pack --dry-run` on a clean LF archive of this head: **105 files**, 226,206 bytes packed, 701,707 unpacked. Breakdown: `dist/` 91, `bin/` 7, `scripts/` 2 (init-pai, value-events), `lib/interview.js` 1, plus README, CHANGELOG, LICENSE and package.json. **`extension/`: 0 files. `app/` and `components/`: 0 files.**\n\n## Sean's steps\n1. Dry run: `gh workflow run publish-sdk.yml -R DealAppSeo/trustshell --ref claude/cc1-2026-10-14-release-1.7.0 -f dry_run=true`. Check that the run summary reads: credential VERIFIED, version 1.7.0, dist-tag latest, no release hold.\n2. Publish: `git fetch origin && git tag -a v1.7.0 4bc3bf865b66208e6399f7316e542daa9d5efc1a -m \"@hyperdag/trustshell 1.7.0\" && git push origin v1.7.0`. Pushing the tag is the publish, so do not also run a non-dry dispatch.\n3. Verify:\n   - `npm view @hyperdag/trustshell version dist-tags.latest` should show 1.7.0;\n   - `npx -y @hyperdag/trustshell@1.7.0 --version` should print 1.7.0.\n4. Mark this PR ready and merge it. Then merge hyperdag-protocol#58, the BUILDERS.md bump.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
